WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.550
Alexander Wang: I don't
think there is any occasion

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:03.330
that all black isn't appropriate for.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:05.060
Like, if there is, I don't go to it.

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:06.770
[Narrator] Today we're
talking to Alexander Wang

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:08.880
about styling all-black outfits.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.070
We'll be talking about
the textures, proportions,

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:15.370
and accessories that keep
all-black fits interesting.

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:19.960
Black has been a cornerstone
of Alexander Wang's brand

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:21.333
and personal style.

00:00:21.333 --> 00:00:23.240
So, Alex, why the black?

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.475
Wang: In my personal style,

00:00:24.475 --> 00:00:28.510
I'd say that it's just,
it's easy, it's versatile.

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:30.840
Whether I'm going to work
or I'm going to the gym

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.450
or I'm going out right after work,

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:34.090
or, you know, I'm going to
another kind of meeting,

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:35.750
I think a black T-shirt
and a black pair of jeans

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:37.990
kind of really, essentially,
you can kind of win

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:39.685
in any situation with that.

00:00:39.685 --> 00:00:41.480
Most situations.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.130
I think in work as well, it
just creates this attitude,

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:46.270
immediate attitude, you know,
when I look at something

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:48.450
in black, and I think it's also
kind of like a blank slate.

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:50.590
When I do use color or
print, things like that,

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:53.130
there has to be a really
strong purpose and reason

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:56.520
and story why I'm using
fuchsia or turquoise.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:57.815
We're not a colorful brand.

00:00:57.815 --> 00:00:59.442
With black, it's kind of like the canvas.

00:00:59.442 --> 00:01:03.083
It's just, you know,
it's kind of what really

00:01:03.083 --> 00:01:05.466
wraps up the entire kind of emotionality

00:01:05.466 --> 00:01:07.420
around what our brand stands for.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:09.600
I think the best way to wear all black

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.130
is to really mix up your
textures and your proportions.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:15.660
[Narrator] So what are textures,
and how do you pair them?

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.230
Wang: Texture.

00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:19.900
I mean, I'm wearing black
jersey and black denim

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:22.060
and charcoal socks right now.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:26.340
Today I did decide to wear
leopard pony-hair shoes.

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.150
Usually I'm wearing kind
of, like, black sneakers

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:29.400
or things like that.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.775
It's not that I always feel like there has

00:01:30.775 --> 00:01:32.470
to be an injection of something

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:34.480
of a print or something
humorous, or, you know,

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:36.820
unexpected in that kind
of outside of black,

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:40.120
but I do think it really
is about how you wear it.

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.412
I think a good pair of black jeans,

00:01:42.412 --> 00:01:43.944
you know, are really important and kind of

00:01:43.944 --> 00:01:47.000
a great, kind of universal piece to have.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.540
[Narrator] And the
proportions, how about those?

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:51.831
Wang: I mean, obviously it applies

00:01:51.831 --> 00:01:54.022
differently for each person.

00:01:54.022 --> 00:01:56.300
I think it's really about knowing

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.230
your body type and kind of how to wear

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:00.780
certain kinds of archetypes or materials

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.280
that kind of exemplify your attitude

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:04.260
and your sensibility.

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:05.960
I tend to wear things a little bit looser,

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:08.060
a little bit more oversized,
'cause I do like things

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:09.650
that feel a little bit more offbeat,

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:12.700
a little bit more casual,
in every situation.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:15.160
So even my blazers are
a bit more unstructured,

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:16.750
you know, my pants are
a little bit looser,

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:18.660
the crotch is a little bit more dropped.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:21.691
I think it really depends
who the person is.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:28.760
Sometimes black can feel very
strict, very buttoned-up,

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:31.330
you know, whether you're
wearing a tight black turtleneck

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:32.838
and kind of leggings,
and things like that,

00:02:32.838 --> 00:02:34.978
which is also something that
we've done in the brand,

00:02:34.978 --> 00:02:36.573
but kind of how you layer
it up and, you know,

00:02:36.573 --> 00:02:37.885
throwing kind of a big sweater

00:02:37.885 --> 00:02:39.640
or a big kind of, you know, cardigan

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.500
or a jacket over it really kind of changes

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:42.970
that attitude immediately.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:47.590
I never like to dictate,
because I just don't think

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:49.210
there's any rules anymore.

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:50.460
You know, there really aren't.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.240
You know, I might say that
right now and somebody might

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:56.217
come in in a skin-tight black
outfit, and I'd be like,

00:02:56.217 --> 00:02:58.200
"Oh, [bleep], she looks great."

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.370
[Narrator] So how do you accessorize?

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:01.880
Wang: I'm really into gold.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:03.620
I was a very, a silver person.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.290
Now I'm very into gold as I get older.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:07.650
So maybe that's it.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:08.900
Evolution of myself.

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:12.157
Honestly, there's never been
an occasion where I felt like,

00:03:12.157 --> 00:03:14.970
oh my gosh, you know, like,
is all black too much?

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:17.510
I didn't follow the
instructions today, by the way.

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:19.542
They told me specifically
not to wear black,

00:03:19.542 --> 00:03:22.060
and of course just by
default I threw on black

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:24.060
and came here, and someone on my team

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:26.218
reminded me that I didn't listen.

